			<div class="content" id="post-content-4445588">
									

<p>First and foremost, +1 for the twist. Excellent concept, well delivered, didn't overstay it's welcome. I do have to agree with Roget and Rounder on this though.</p>
<p>The containment procedures do very little to lead the mystery, and don't really function. If we haven't figured out how to kill these animals, humanely or otherwise, then this is a much bigger issue warranting greater response. As it stands, this feels like &quot;toss them in a pen&quot;. Even the addition of &quot;until a solution can be devised&quot; would have made this feel more complete. A unique method of eliminating these animals using anomalous, or just Foundation level technology would have closed the loop as well without subtracting from the story.</p>
<p>The dialogue feels stilted, unprofessional, and lacks a cohesive tone. You also go a bit too hard on the accent with &quot;them&quot; and whatnot. The impact of &quot;the dog can't die&quot; would have had much more weight if these agents had started off by-the-books, then having that broken by the horror of the situation. The good part is the actual skeleton is strong: the shock of the dog not dying after multiple gunshots is well executed and paced.</p>
<p>It's still a +1 for sure, but it needs to be tightened. Good work McB.</p>

							</div>

								
					
